VirtIO GPU: Follow the host size of scanout 0 with the primary framebuffer

On a display event whose scanout 0 size is new and between 640x480 and 3840x2160, replace the framebuffer through the mode change path. Display events, client mode sets, client scanout resources and presenter flips change scanout 0 one at a time. A size outside the mode list is mode 0x100, so the listed mode ids stay, and the framebuffer connection counts and copies the mode ids in one step. A refused step keeps the old mode and sets its scanout again. A SET_SCANOUT without a reply keeps both framebuffers and the old mode, and the old scanout is set again before any later change. Framebuffer connections read a generation that advances with each new framebuffer. Add the replacement steps and the mode ids as a header with a host test.

